PS5 HDMI: the HDMI chip is an HDMI endpoint, no 6 bpc; 4K120 as YCbCr 4:2:2 (v1.8.4)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

hsgodd's log on v1.8.3: "3840x2160@120 over FRL (RGB, 6 bpc)". amdgpu's encoding selection
skips 6 bpc only for HDMI sinks and DP->HDMI dongles; the PS5's HDMI chip is a DP->HDMI
converter but doesn't report as a dongle, so 4K120 went out as RGB at 6 bpc (fits the DP link)
instead of YCbCr 4:2:2 at 8 bpc, the format Sony's 4K120 setup for the chip (Lawson's port)
is made for, and his LG showed no picture. The PS5's HDMI connector now counts as the HDMI
endpoint it is: RGB 8 bpc where it fits, else YCbCr 4:2:2; never 6 bpc.
---

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -2428,6 +2428,16 @@
 		     aconnector->dc_link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type ==
 			     DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER);
 	is_dp_or_hdmi = dc_is_hdmi_signal(signal) || dc_is_dp_signal(signal);
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_PS5
+	/*
+	 * v1.8.4: the PS5's HDMI chip is a DP->HDMI converter, but doesn't report itself as a
+	 * dongle, so 4K120 went out as RGB at 6 bpc (fits the DP link; HDMI has no 6 bpc) instead
+	 * of YCbCr 4:2:2 at 8 bpc, which the chip's 4K120 setup (Sony's) is made for. On
+	 * hsgodd's LG that gave no picture. Treat it as the HDMI endpoint it is.
+	 */
+	if (ps5_dm_is_hdmi_connector(aconnector))
+		is_hdmi_ep = true;
+#endif
 
